Protobuf files given by Saheed Rosenje from the Telematics E2E Team:
Payload.proto

To generate code from that, we need the correct version of the tools.

There are already build and released version of protoc and grpc plugin in lib_oss/grpc-a

These are tagged along with the libraries and includes for the target platform, so you will certainly be in sync.

I cloned this into ~/git/a6n2

$ git clone git@git1.corp.cat.com:/oss/grpc-a
$ cd grpc-a
$ git checkout grpc_v1.0.0_2018.1.0

In order to make sure *this* toolchain is used instead of anything installed on the local host, make sure to call the 'protoc' script:

$ cd tgt_gcc_4.4.3_ubuntu/protoc/
$ cat protoc
#/bin/sh
SCRIPT=$(readlink -f $0)
BASE_PATH=`dirname $SCRIPT`
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$BASE_PATH:$BASE_PATH/../lib/
$BASE_PATH/protoc-bin "$@"

Example:

$ ~/git/a6n2/grpc-a/tgt_gcc_4.4.3_ubuntu/protoc/protoc Payload.proto --cpp_out=./
